      "text": "SGLang (Structured Generation Language) is an open-source high-performance inference framework for large language models developed by the SGLang project (sgl-project). It provides a frontend language for expressing complex LLM programs — including multi-turn chat, tool use, and structured output — and a backend runtime with optimized kernels, continuous batching, tensor parallelism, and memory-efficient attention. SGLang is used to serve models such as Llama, Qwen, and DeepSeek at scale in production environments, competing with frameworks like vLLM and TensorRT-LLM."
