    "summary": "SGLang reached its 1.0 stability milestone this week, marked by a summit where Cloudflare and LinkedIn detailed production deployments serving over 10,000 queries per second with sub-80-millisecond latency. The release hardens the inference framework's APIs, replaces silent configuration changes with explicit errors, and defines a compatibility policy for the 1.x series. Meanwhile, DeepSeek open-sourced DeepInfer, its high-performance inference engine supporting DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash with optimized kernels, MoE expert parallelism, and asynchronous scheduling. Thinking Machines published Inkling-2-Small, a multimodal model for agentic and retrieval-augmented workloads. The broader community also rallied around a \"No AI Slop\" manifesto signed by conference speakers, emphasizing quality standards for generated content.",
